      "ESG Ratings Methodology | March 2026\nTYPE OF RISK/\nTIME HORIZON\nOPPORTUNITY\nShort Med Long\nDemand Shift Acute Demand Shift: Demonstrated Demand Forecast Demand Shift:\nOngoing demand shift Shift: Growing demand Underlying social or\nbetween substitute in “new” area evidenced environmental pressures\nproducts/services, old by differential growth (e.g., obese population,\nproduct/service rates and notable shift in climate change) are\nbecoming obsolete. market share between likely to cause change in\nsubstitutes. demand and consumer\npreference over time.\nIncentive-Based\nDemand Shift: Demand Competitor Response:\nshift over 2- to 5-year Major industry player(s)\nperiod will be led by undertake strategic\ngovernment incentives. response to\nenvironmental or social\ntrends, increasing\ncompetitive pressure.\n© 2026 MSCI Inc. All rights reserved. Please refer to the disclaimer at the end of this document. msci.com Page 46 of 60",
      "ESG Ratings Methodology | March 2026\nAppendix 4: ESG Rating Industries\nESG Rating Industries are based on GICS sub-industries, where applicable, which MSCI S&C groups to\nform peer sets in which companies face relatively similar Key Issues. As a result, each ESG Rating\nIndustry can be mapped to a GICS sub-industry, a GICS Industry or several GICS sub-industries.14\nCompanies are assigned to ESG Rating Industries based on the company’s GICS classification (if\navailable) or based on MSCI S&C’s determination if no GICS classification is available (e.g., private or\nunlisted companies).\n• Key Issues and Key Issue Weights are determined at the GICS sub-industry level.\n• Industry-Adjusted Scores and ESG letter ratings are relative within each ESG Rating Industry.\n• Percentiles, quartiles, averages and score distributions on reports are calculated relative to the\nESG Rating Industry.\nESG Rating Industry GICS Sub-industry\nENERGY\nEnergy Equipment & Services 10101010 Oil & Gas Drilling\n10101020 Oil & Gas Equipment & Services\nIntegrated Oil & Gas 10102010 Integrated Oil & Gas\nOil & Gas Exploration &\n10102020 Oil & Gas Exploration & Production\nProduction\nOil & Gas Refining, Marketing,\n10102030 Oil & Gas Refining & Marketing\nTransportation & Storage\n10102040 Oil & Gas Storage & Transportation\nMATERIALS\nMetals and Mining - Non-\n10102050 Coal & Consumable Fuels\nPrecious Metals\n15104010 Aluminum\n15104020 Diversified Metals & Mining\n15104025 Copper\nCommodity & Diversified\n15101010 Commodity Chemicals\nChemicals\n15101020 Diversified Chemicals\nSpecialty Chemicals 15101030 Fertilizers & Agricultural Chemicals\n15101040 Industrial Gases\n15101050 Specialty Chemicals\nConstruction Materials 15102010 Construction Materials\n14 With the exception of supranationals and development banks, which are not covered in the GICS framework.\n© 2026 MSCI Inc. All rights reserved. Please refer to the disclaimer at the end of this document. msci.com Page 47 of 60",
